Port the ssv6158 driver to Linux 6.18.

Build with ccflags-y and without Android wakelocks.
Use kernel_read/kernel_write, proc_ops, and the renamed timer API.
Follow the mac80211 vif->cfg, deflink, link_id, and radio_idx changes.
Add the TX queue and channel context ops that mac80211 requires.
Read the config from /lib/firmware/ssv6158-wifi.cfg.
Load SSV6020 firmware as ssv6020-sw.bin. SSV6006 already uses ssv6x5x-sw.bin.
Drop the exports. The driver is one module, and the names clash with ssv6051.

